WEBVTT

00:00.637 --> 00:03.517
Hey, you. Wanna team up 
with a dependable front liner?

00:03.517 --> 00:04.487
Are you sure you're strong?

00:07.437 --> 00:09.967
<i>A Fang of Smoldering
 Insanity skillbook.</i>

00:08.207 --> 00:15.587
<b>Fang of 
Smoldering Insanity</b>

00:09.497 --> 00:15.587
<b>Skillbook</b>

00:10.567 --> 00:15.007
<i>Skillbooks are items required 
to unlock skill trees.</i>

00:15.957 --> 00:19.587
<i>They're rare, 
so I won't find one right away,</i>

00:20.057 --> 00:22.067
<i>but looking for one is free.</i>

00:23.597 --> 00:25.847
<b>Remaining skill points: 5</b>

00:23.597 --> 00:25.847
<b>Oath of the Heavy Armor</b>

00:23.597 --> 00:25.847
<b>Defense Booster</b>

00:23.597 --> 00:25.847
<b>Beginner Swordsmanship</b>

00:24.017 --> 00:28.107
<i>Oath of the Heavy Armor 
and Fang of Smoldering Insanity.</i>

00:28.107 --> 00:32.287
<i>These two skill trees work together 
to complete the Heavy Knight.</i>

00:34.297 --> 00:38.947
<i>The completed Heavy Knight 
is no longer a defense specialist.</i>

00:38.947 --> 00:41.857
<i>Even calling it an offensive specialist
 isn't right either.</i>

00:41.857 --> 00:45.107
<i>It's a human weapon.</i>

00:46.747 --> 00:52.997
<i>Fang of Smoldering Insanity is essential
 to unlocking the Heavy Knight's potential.</i>

01:37.377 --> 01:38.627
<b>Loading</b>

01:49.887 --> 01:51.197
<b>Loading</b>

02:02.527 --> 02:03.817
<b>Loading</b>

02:12.077 --> 02:12.827
<b>Loading</b>

02:14.327 --> 02:19.917
<b>Begin Adventure</b>

02:14.327 --> 02:19.917
<b>Begin Adventure</b>

02:31.097 --> 02:35.557
<b>Episode 5</b>

02:31.097 --> 02:35.557
<b>Fang of Smoldering 
Insanity</b>

02:40.487 --> 02:44.137
Whoa, she's cute... 
but out of my league.

02:58.877 --> 03:00.257
Don't waste it.

03:00.257 --> 03:02.877
I know. Thanks, Dad.

03:03.517 --> 03:08.637
<i>A Fang of Smoldering Insanity skillbook 
is a key item for the Heavy Knight.</i>

03:08.957 --> 03:12.897
<i>It'd be great if I could find one 
in this city.</i>

03:37.767 --> 03:38.667
Excuse me.

03:39.327 --> 03:41.367
Could I get three healing potions?

03:41.367 --> 03:44.777
Sure thing. That'll be 72,000 gold.

03:46.327 --> 03:49.527
<i>That's a lot more 
expensive than in the game.</i>

03:50.177 --> 03:53.677
<i>That said, there's no way around it.</i>

03:54.197 --> 03:55.487
Fine.

03:57.317 --> 03:59.857
By the way, I have a question.

04:00.777 --> 04:02.897
Where can I buy skillbooks?

04:03.307 --> 04:04.527
Oh...

04:05.327 --> 04:08.417
I couldn't find any at any shops.

04:09.287 --> 04:12.547
<i>A Heavy Knight is stuck 
in tutorial mode until</i>

04:10.157 --> 04:10.657
<b>Yah!</b>

04:10.157 --> 04:10.987
<b>Croak</b>

04:12.157 --> 04:12.657
<b>Yah!</b>

04:12.157 --> 04:13.027
<b>Skree</b>

04:12.547 --> 04:14.617
<i>they find a Fang of 
Smoldering Insanity skillbook.</i>

04:14.617 --> 04:16.417
<i>I have to get my hands on one.</i>

04:14.907 --> 04:16.407
<b>Yes!</b>

04:16.737 --> 04:19.287
You don't know anything, do you?

04:19.287 --> 04:20.117
Huh?

04:20.507 --> 04:24.997
Are you a first-year adventurer 
who just got his class?

04:24.997 --> 04:26.337
Y-Yeah.

04:26.997 --> 04:30.297
Buying and selling 
skillbooks is prohibited.

04:30.637 --> 04:31.677
What?

04:31.677 --> 04:35.867
People are permitted 
to use skillbooks they acquire,

04:35.867 --> 04:41.847
but otherwise, the Adventurer's Guild
 gives them to nobles and the church.

04:41.847 --> 04:44.607
Y-You're kidding, right?!

04:45.147 --> 04:49.247
<i>Skillbooks are an unbelievably rare drop.</i>

04:49.247 --> 04:50.607
<i>It's assumed you'll have to buy them.</i>

04:51.077 --> 04:55.117
<i>You can't expect to find the one you want.</i>

04:55.547 --> 05:01.327
<i>I did feel that nobles were more powerful
than they were in the game, but...</i>

05:02.067 --> 05:04.947
<i>I can't believe this is happening.</i>

05:05.747 --> 05:10.257
<i>It's likely that my family, the Edvaughns,</i>

05:10.257 --> 05:14.367
<i>have all the skillbooks 
collected in Rondalm.</i>

05:17.847 --> 05:19.847
Oh, fine.

05:19.847 --> 05:24.857
I'm not supposed to tell you this, 
but I'll make an exception.

05:24.857 --> 05:27.507
You know, since you bought 
the healing potions.

05:31.077 --> 05:33.777
Here. Go to this place.

05:35.917 --> 05:36.947
What's this?

05:39.227 --> 05:42.077
A shop that deals in scavenged goods.

05:42.437 --> 05:45.587
<i>Scavengers. Are those people 
who loot dead adventurers?</i>

05:46.577 --> 05:53.047
Aren't those items supposed to be 
reported to the Adventurer's Guild?

05:53.617 --> 05:56.187
They have an unspoken agreement.

05:56.187 --> 06:00.677
The guild knows about these 
underground shops and leaves them be.

06:01.467 --> 06:05.847
Some adventurers can't 
survive without scavenging.

06:06.227 --> 06:08.857
Besides, even if they followed 
standard procedure,

06:09.317 --> 06:13.967
most items would end up in the hands of 
nobles instead of their surviving family.

06:15.297 --> 06:21.327
Nobles buy up skillbooks for cheap 
and hoard them instead of using them.

06:21.677 --> 06:24.327
They don't know how hard 
it is to be an adventurer.

06:27.747 --> 06:30.837
<i>I was utterly naive.</i>

06:31.677 --> 06:34.077
<i>If my memories 
of my past life hadn't returned,</i>

06:34.077 --> 06:36.837
<i>and I'd become a Master Swordsman...</i>

06:36.837 --> 06:41.527
Don't tell the mucky-mucks 
about this shop.

06:41.527 --> 06:43.297
Of course.

06:47.407 --> 06:53.127
<i>I'd rather die than tell anyone 
I'm a noble's son.</i>

07:08.957 --> 07:11.077
We're partners now!

08:01.227 --> 08:04.567
<i>Do they really have skillbooks here?</i>

08:09.637 --> 08:12.347
<i>They do. Five, even.</i>

08:12.977 --> 08:14.977
That's some dinky armor.

08:17.417 --> 08:23.227
This Hall of Broken Grimoires 
isn't for newbies like you.

08:24.897 --> 08:29.407
I have gold. Could I see your Skillbooks?

08:29.407 --> 08:31.377
You're welcome to look.

08:31.377 --> 08:35.877
Your filthy fingerprints won't 
make them any less valuable.

08:36.947 --> 08:38.097
Thanks.

08:43.087 --> 08:45.387
<i>Beginner Archery Skillbook.</i>

08:44.557 --> 08:48.177
<b>Beginner Archery
Market Price: 2,000,000G</b>

08:45.387 --> 08:47.847
<i>Market price: two million gold.</i>

08:48.737 --> 08:50.447
<i>Two million gold?!</i>

08:50.447 --> 08:53.937
<i>That's 500,000 gold more 
expensive than the game!</i>

08:54.267 --> 08:59.647
<i>In the game, the market price was based 
on trades made between players.</i>

09:00.517 --> 09:06.027
<i>This price is probably based 
on actual trade prices, too.</i>

09:06.467 --> 09:11.367
<i>The price of skillbooks must be inflated 
due to nobles hoarding them.</i>

09:12.037 --> 09:16.247
Just so you know, I'd charge 
three million gold for that.

09:16.247 --> 09:18.507
Th-Three million?!

09:18.507 --> 09:22.637
Of course. This is a risky 
business I'm running.

09:22.637 --> 09:26.467
The officials look the other way,

09:26.467 --> 09:30.557
but if their superiors find out, 
I could lose my head.

09:36.917 --> 09:40.787
<i>Basic beginner skillbooks 
are this expensive...</i>

09:42.427 --> 09:47.707
<i>Even if I sell the Daemonsrage Shield,
I'll only have three million gold.</i>

09:45.277 --> 09:48.077
<b>Current Funds: Approx. 900,000G</b>

09:48.757 --> 09:53.077
<i>I doubt that's enough 
to buy a rare skillbook.</i>

10:00.427 --> 10:06.227
<i>Beginner Archery, Magic Booster, 
Jack-in-the-Box, and Elemental Guard.</i>

10:07.097 --> 10:12.097
<i>They're pretty rare, but they're 
not what I'm looking for.</i>

10:12.677 --> 10:14.767
<i>What's this last one?</i>

10:24.207 --> 10:25.687
<i>This is it!</i>

10:27.687 --> 10:31.527
<i>The skill tree essential to Heavy Knight, 
Fang of Smoldering Insanity!</i>

10:31.527 --> 10:34.247
<i>Once I have this, I'm golden!</i>

10:34.247 --> 10:37.717
What's this? You look awfully happy.

10:38.227 --> 10:42.067
You must be an oddball if you want that.

10:42.067 --> 10:44.307
Ma'am, this book...

10:46.377 --> 10:49.347
I'd charge fifty million gold for that.

10:49.347 --> 10:50.237
Fifty...

11:00.477 --> 11:04.397
I'm amazed you keep such expensive 
merchandise out without any guards.

11:05.537 --> 11:09.177
If you think I'm weak, try me.

11:09.177 --> 11:11.787
I threw five guys out on 
their asses the other day.

11:21.287 --> 11:25.667
Could you hold onto this skillbook for me?

11:26.317 --> 11:29.267
I promise I'll come back 
with fifty million gold.

11:37.917 --> 11:41.347
What's in it for me?

11:41.347 --> 11:43.937
What? Well, uh...

11:45.117 --> 11:47.737
I don't dislike kids like you.

11:47.737 --> 11:48.487
Huh?

11:50.797 --> 11:53.257
Sure. I'll hold onto it.

11:54.217 --> 11:55.347
Really?

11:55.347 --> 11:56.387
Sure.

11:59.077 --> 12:01.847
For an extra five million gold.

12:02.967 --> 12:05.547
<i>She drives a hard bargain.</i>

12:10.797 --> 12:14.397
<i>I'll be finding ways 
to make money for a while.</i>

12:21.307 --> 12:23.487
How'd it go with them?

12:24.047 --> 12:25.777
I'd like to team up again.

12:30.137 --> 12:31.847
I put my own spin on it.

12:32.587 --> 12:34.367
That is so cute.

12:42.147 --> 12:44.667
<i>Fifty-five million gold, huh?</i>

12:44.667 --> 12:48.627
<i>That's sixty times what I made 
from that raid quest.</i>

12:49.617 --> 12:53.427
<i>High-level adventurers 
and the shops they deal with</i>

12:53.427 --> 12:55.797
<i>have a busted perspective of wealth.</i>

12:57.117 --> 13:00.907
<i>Fang of Smoldering Insanity 
is a rare skill tree,</i>

13:00.907 --> 13:03.447
<i>but the only ones who want it are</i>

13:03.447 --> 13:07.327
<i>Heavy Knights and combat junkies 
with a death wish.</i>

13:08.377 --> 13:13.107
<i>More obviously powerful skillbooks 
must be absurdly expensive.</i>

13:13.847 --> 13:17.117
<i>I have to come up with practical 
ways to make money.</i>

13:18.117 --> 13:21.917
<i>I could try to get rich quick 
by farming rare drops in dungeons.</i>

13:19.117 --> 13:21.917
<b>All right!</b>

13:22.417 --> 13:27.207
<i>No, Heavy Knights don't have skills 
to deal consistent damage.</i>

13:22.957 --> 13:27.917
<b>Roar</b>

13:23.457 --> 13:27.917
<b>Aaah</b>

13:26.877 --> 13:27.917
<b>Impossible</b>

13:28.477 --> 13:30.607
<i>I could farm weak monsters 
with Rampart Reflection.</i>

13:28.667 --> 13:31.087
<b>Hmph!!</b>

13:28.917 --> 13:31.087
<b>Croak</b>

13:28.917 --> 13:31.087
<b>Croak</b>

13:28.917 --> 13:31.087
<b>Croak</b>

13:31.467 --> 13:31.837
<b>Hmph</b>

13:32.087 --> 13:32.467
<b>Hmph</b>

13:32.607 --> 13:35.007
<i>That would take too long.</i>

13:32.717 --> 13:33.087
<b>Hmph</b>

13:33.337 --> 13:33.717
<b>Hmph</b>

13:33.967 --> 13:34.337
<b>Hmph</b>

13:34.587 --> 13:34.967
<b>Hmph</b>

13:35.047 --> 13:36.097
<b>Impossible</b>

13:36.097 --> 13:38.217
<b>Attack Skills</b>

13:36.097 --> 13:37.087
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:36.567 --> 13:38.047
<i>I could use Beginner Swordsmanship</i>

13:37.087 --> 13:38.217
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:38.047 --> 13:41.057
<i>or find another Skillbook 
and build up those skill trees.</i>

13:38.217 --> 13:39.337
<b>Attack Skills</b>

13:38.217 --> 13:39.337
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:39.337 --> 13:41.507
<b>Attack Skills</b>

13:39.337 --> 13:41.507
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:42.147 --> 13:47.537
<i>No, I'd stop using them once I acquired 
Fang of Smoldering Insanity.</i>

13:48.107 --> 13:50.107
<b>Attack Skills</b>

13:48.107 --> 13:48.597
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:48.597 --> 13:50.107
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:48.827 --> 13:51.617
<i>I'd like to avoid wasting skill points.</i>

13:50.107 --> 13:52.607
<b>Attack Skills</b>

13:50.107 --> 13:52.607
<b>Beginner
 Swordsmanship</b>

13:51.317 --> 13:52.607
<b>Impossible</b>

13:55.337 --> 13:58.857
He's a veteran adventurer, 
and I was so rude to him.

13:58.857 --> 14:00.077
Again?!

14:00.907 --> 14:03.917
<i>Heavy Knights aren't popular,</i>

14:03.917 --> 14:07.037
<i>but that raid quest should've 
gotten my name out there.</i>

14:07.037 --> 14:10.737
<i>I'd have a lot more options 
if I teamed up with other adventurers.</i>

14:11.677 --> 14:12.967
Allies...

14:16.007 --> 14:20.597
I-I'll keep it busy while you run.

14:29.977 --> 14:33.197
You doubt Elymas?

14:33.197 --> 14:38.027
Then you're insulting me 
for approving his promotion!

14:38.867 --> 14:41.057
I guess I'll find allies.

14:42.437 --> 14:47.587
Man, I wasn't expecting 
a Blood-Soaked Sword to drop.

14:49.787 --> 14:52.547
The market price is two million gold.

14:52.547 --> 14:55.427
We can have fun with that for a while.

15:01.027 --> 15:05.117
It's because of my skills, you know.

15:06.347 --> 15:09.807
<b>Silence...</b>

15:07.917 --> 15:08.907
What?

15:12.937 --> 15:17.007
They worked, didn't they?

15:18.267 --> 15:21.947
<i>A Swordsman, a Bandit, and a Pierrot?</i>

15:23.227 --> 15:25.827
Because of you, huh?

15:26.957 --> 15:31.707
We finally got this rare drop after 
visiting the dungeon a bunch of times.

15:32.037 --> 15:36.717
I'm not sure that it really was 
because of your skills.

15:38.487 --> 15:40.387
No, you're right.

15:40.387 --> 15:46.267
B-But if we visit more dungeons, 
you'll start to see the difference.

15:46.267 --> 15:48.277
We're just getting started.

15:48.277 --> 15:50.467
Don't tell me, Ruche...

15:53.687 --> 15:58.557
You're so weak. Do you really think 
you'll get a cut of the sale?

15:59.477 --> 16:00.327
What?

16:06.867 --> 16:08.037
But...

16:08.267 --> 16:12.037
But I risk my life fighting 
on the front line, too.

16:12.427 --> 16:14.447
At least give me a fifth.

16:14.447 --> 16:16.457
No, wait. 200,000...

16:16.457 --> 16:20.407
A hundred thousand gold would be nice.

16:20.407 --> 16:21.087
What?

16:21.087 --> 16:22.547
Just kidding.

16:24.707 --> 16:27.727
Listen, you may be risking your life,

16:27.727 --> 16:29.467
but you don't have 
any decent attack skills.

16:29.467 --> 16:34.277
You just soak up some hits. 
That's the problem.

16:35.747 --> 16:38.147
You're not actually useful.

16:49.917 --> 16:53.097
I-I don't have attack skills...

16:55.537 --> 16:59.717
because I assigned my skill points 
like you told me to.

16:59.717 --> 17:00.907
What?

17:01.947 --> 17:07.807
D-Don't you think it's mean to say that 
once we've made a bunch of money?

17:08.427 --> 17:10.307
Mean?

17:11.327 --> 17:14.847
Mean, huh?

17:17.147 --> 17:20.067
I think you're confused.

17:21.447 --> 17:27.447
Reducing our take 
when you're useless is a problem.

17:27.447 --> 17:29.947
Besides, I just made a little suggestion.

17:29.947 --> 17:33.477
You're the one who actually 
assigned your skill points.

17:33.957 --> 17:40.607
Now you're blaming me and demanding 
a share when you've contributed nothing.

17:40.607 --> 17:42.067
Mr. Cline?

17:42.927 --> 17:47.467
<i>A bad build and argument 
over how to split the treasure.</i>

17:47.787 --> 17:51.587
<i>That happened all the time 
in </i>Magic World<i>, too.</i>

17:47.787 --> 17:49.557
This isn't what we agreed to!

17:49.557 --> 17:51.587
That's your problem!

17:51.587 --> 17:55.637
<i>You assign your skill points 
to fit your party,</i>

17:55.637 --> 17:57.907
<i>but the situation changes, 
and your choices become meaningless.</i>

17:57.907 --> 17:59.067
Fine, fine.

17:59.527 --> 18:00.797
Here.

18:03.057 --> 18:04.697
That's 100,000 gold.

18:06.777 --> 18:08.577
This is what you wanted, right?

18:08.577 --> 18:10.847
Pick it up and get out of here.

18:11.807 --> 18:16.847
We kept you around even though you're 
weak and don't have decent attack skills,

18:17.477 --> 18:21.737
and now you're showing your true colors 
because you're blinded by chump change.

18:21.737 --> 18:23.037
Right, Reiss?

18:24.127 --> 18:26.007
Don't you agree?

18:29.227 --> 18:31.247
I guess so.

18:34.137 --> 18:39.517
It's not like we can afford to share 
the wealth we happened to acquire.

18:39.517 --> 18:42.217
Th-That's not what I meant!

18:42.217 --> 18:45.567
I'm sorry, Mr. Cline and Ms. Reiss!

18:46.027 --> 18:49.527
I actually don't need 
any gold for the sword!

18:49.527 --> 18:51.447
Sorry doesn't cut it.

18:52.397 --> 18:53.997
We just can't anymore.

18:57.807 --> 19:00.897
Well, good luck with your next party.

19:00.897 --> 19:04.277
Though I don't know who'd recruit a loser

19:04.277 --> 19:09.277
who can't level up anymore 
because of their bad build.

19:11.437 --> 19:15.307
<i>They say relationships only last 
as long as the money does.</i>

19:15.917 --> 19:19.287
<i>The skill point system is brutal.</i>

19:20.237 --> 19:27.647
<i>You have to farm monsters at or above 
your level to get any decent experience.</i>

19:28.867 --> 19:31.957
You don't have any decent attack skills.

19:31.957 --> 19:36.657
You just soak up some hits. 
That's the problem.

19:36.657 --> 19:38.927
You're not actually useful.

19:40.537 --> 19:46.417
<i>But if your build is bad and you 
struggle against enemies your level,</i>

19:46.417 --> 19:50.427
<b>Nooo!</b>

19:46.417 --> 19:50.427
<b>Nooo!</b>

19:46.667 --> 19:47.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:46.667 --> 19:47.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:47.177 --> 19:50.427
<i>raising your level becomes 
incredibly difficult.</i>

19:47.677 --> 19:48.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:47.677 --> 19:48.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:48.677 --> 19:49.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:48.677 --> 19:49.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:49.677 --> 19:50.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:49.677 --> 19:50.177
<b>Croak!</b>

19:53.957 --> 19:59.807
<i>Did she put her points in Speed Booster 
or a weapon skill tree she doesn't need?</i>

20:01.087 --> 20:03.567
<i>Since she's a Pierrot, 
is it a support tree?</i>

20:05.757 --> 20:08.277
I wasn't expecting 
a Blood-Soaked Sword to drop.

20:15.507 --> 20:19.487
It's because of my skills, you know.

20:23.937 --> 20:27.957
They worked, didn't they?

20:30.137 --> 20:32.617
Because of you, huh?

20:33.717 --> 20:38.347
We finally got this rare drop after 
visiting the dungeon a bunch of times.

20:38.697 --> 20:42.997
I'm not sure that it really was 
because of your skills.

20:43.997 --> 20:45.187
<i>Could it be?</i>

20:46.177 --> 20:48.277
<i>Does she have that skill tree?</i>

20:48.697 --> 20:52.277
<i>Who'd kick someone with </i>that<i> skill tree?</i>

20:52.277 --> 20:54.947
<i>But based on that conversation, 
that must be it.</i>

20:55.427 --> 21:00.457
<i>If I'm right, she's got 
a broken skill tree.</i>

21:02.077 --> 21:04.627
I'm sorry for being selfish!

21:04.987 --> 21:06.867
You never have to pay me again!

21:06.867 --> 21:10.127
Please keep me in the party!

21:13.927 --> 21:16.027
Wh-Who are you?!

21:16.027 --> 21:16.977
Please!

21:22.047 --> 21:26.427
Please! Will you form a party with me?

21:27.217 --> 21:29.817
A p-p-party?!

21:56.047 --> 21:59.557
<b>Translator:
